name issue_61_googcc_glue_congestive
describe Congestive loss with every v2 switch on: GoogCC's glue (pacing 1.1 x target, padding, overhead rate, cwnd drop through the allocator) keeps the sender at its target (#61)
cc v2
pacer v2
tcc v2
rtx v2
rtcp v2
keyframe v2
allocator v2
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=30ms queue=60ms
at 15s capacity=800kbps
# Seeds 1-5, all v2 switches: net.loss_pct main 11.0 -> 4.3 (libwebrtc 4.5), cc.send_over_target_ms 3860 -> 100
# (libwebrtc 60), cc.utilization_pct 82 -> 91 (libwebrtc 91), video.avg_kbps 1015 -> 1148 (libwebrtc 1182).
# Freezes rise (2.4 -> 3.2 s; libwebrtc 2.1 s) and are owned by #61's flip (keyframe/NACK recovery).
# Port (#150, RobustThroughputEstimator as the acked-rate estimator, as libwebrtc M157), on top of #124's audio phase
# (#180): net.loss_pct over seeds 1-10 is 3.7-6.3 (mean 4.9; seed 1 4.4), against libwebrtc's 2.7-5.8 (mean 4.5).
expect net.loss_pct < 7
expect cc.send_over_target_ms < 1000
expect cc.utilization_pct > 86
expect video.avg_kbps > 1080
